# Accepted-risk signal-disposition sites excluded from the ownership gate.
#
# Format: file:line:hash  # rationale
#   file    = repo-relative path
#   line    = line number of the flagged call as reported by the scanner
#   hash    = first 8 hex chars of sha256 of the both-ends-trimmed line
#             content (leading and trailing whitespace stripped)
#
# Keying on file:line:hash means both the line number AND the site text
# must match.  A renumber or text edit without re-auditing fails on hash
# mismatch.  A new install call added elsewhere in an allowlisted file is
# still caught.

# child/child-init-clean.c: disable_coredumps() debug path.
# Installs SIG_DFL for SIGSEGV so that the kernel generates a real core
# dump when -D is active.  This is intentional: the call site is inside
# the `if (shm->debug == true)` branch whose sole purpose is to undo the
# no-core-dump posture for post-mortem debugging.  No raise() follows;
# no beacon is bypassed.  No canonical snapshot is required because this
# path deliberately drops back to the kernel default rather than chaining
# to a trinity-managed handler.  Audited as locally-balanced: the call
# has no restore counterpart (the child is already in its final setup
# state) and is grandchild-unreachable.
child/child-init-clean.c:83:c735e3c5
